.TH HTTP_RESPONSE_READ 3
.SH NAME
http_response_read \- tell how much body data may be read
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t http_response_read(buffer* " in ", http_response* " response ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_response_read ()
looks at the beginning of the body in
.I in
(without taking it out) and says how many bytes belong to the current piece of the body. For a chunked body it reads the line with the next chunk
size into
.I chunk_length
and sets the status HTTP_STATUS_FINISH at the last chunk, for a body with a length it compares
.I data_pos
with
.I content_length.
.P
This belongs to the first reader of the module, written for
.BR buffer (3)
operations; it expects
.I h->stream
to be cleared. New code should use
.BR http_recv (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes that may be taken now, 0 if there are none (the chunk size is read or missing), 0 for a multipart body (not implemented).
.SH SEE ALSO
http_read_internal(3), http_recv(3)
